 "notes": "95% CL upper limits on g_B-L (hbar c)^{-1/2} (dimensionless gauge coupling of a B-L vector ULDM field) from Fig. 5, digitised from the e-print raster B-LlimitsSimple.png. The paper gives three separate noisy limit curves (491,019 masses) for field polarization along celestial X, Y, Z; reported here is the X-polarization panel, taking per-column the geometric mean of the upper and lower envelopes of the noisy band and median-smoothing into 80 log-spaced mass bins; Y and Z curves agree within ~30%. Axis calibration cross-checked against the top frequency axis (0.1-50 mHz = 0.4136e-18 to 206.8e-18 eV) and the horizontal reference lines (Eot-Wash EP ~1.05e-24, MICROSCOPE ~2.4e-25). Curve minimum ~1.1e-25 at ~8e-18 eV matches the abstract's quoted best limit g_B-L < 1e-25 at 8e-18 eV/c^2. Assumes local DM density rho = 0.3 GeV/cm^3.",
